  "problem": {
    "id": "train-2486",
    "question": "There are 248 pages in a book. Joanna can read 16 pages per hour. On Monday, she reads for 3 hours. On Tuesday, she reads for 6.5 hours. How many more hours does she need to read to finish the book?",
    "gold": "6",
    "answer": "On Monday, Joanna reads 3*16=<<3*16=48>>48 pages.\nOn Tuesday, Joanna reads 6.5 * 16 =<<6.5*16=104>>104 pages.\nSo far, she has read 48 +104 =<<48+104=152>>152 pages.\nThus, she has 248-152 = <<248-152=96>>96 pages left.\nShe will need to read for 96/16 = <<96/16=6>>6 hours to finish the book.\n#### 6"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many more hours Joanna needs to read to finish the book, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of pages Joanna reads on Monday.\n2. Calculate the total number of pages Joanna reads on Tuesday.\n3. Determine the total number of pages Joanna has read so far.\n4. Subtract the total number of pages read from the total number of pages in the book to find out how many more pages she needs to read.\n5. Calculate the number of additional hours Joanna needs to read to finish the book.\n\nLet's start with the calculations:\n\n1. On Monday, Joanna reads for 3 hours at a rate of 16 pages per hour:\n   \\[\n   3 \\text{ hours} \\times 16 \\text{ pages/hour} = 48 \\text{ pages}\n   \\]\n\n2. On Tuesday, Joanna reads for 6.5 hours at a rate of 16 pages per hour:\n   \\[\n   6.5 \\text{ hours} \\times 16 \\text{ pages/hour} = 104 \\text{ pages}\n   \\]\n\n3. The total number of pages Joanna has read so far is:\n   \\[\n   48 \\text{ pages} + 104 \\text{ pages} = 152 \\text{ pages}\n   \\]\n\n4. The total number of pages in the book is 248 pages. The number of pages Joanna still needs to read is:\n   \\[\n   248 \\text{ pages} - 152 \\text{ pages} = 96 \\text{ pages}\n   \\]\n\n5. Since Joanna reads at a rate of 16 pages per hour, the number of additional hours she needs to read to finish the book is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{96 \\text{ pages}}{16 \\text{ pages/hour}} = 6 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of additional hours Joanna needs to read to finish the book is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
